buildUnits.brief:
SCOPE
A worker entry that main selects (S5), never a platform branch inside App.

The entry DOES:
- initialize the engine with fallbackBackendId null and, per D2, no connectProvider;
- load models read-only so resolverHooks resolve (models.ts:396);
- load the MCP servers only if the phone policy allows MCP;
- register the shell tool only if bash is allowed.

The entry does NOT:
- mount App;
- call useChats.load or openChat (the INTERRUPTED sweep at chat.ts:513-528 keys on this renderer's livePlaceholderId, chat.ts:90, and would mark the user window's live row interrupted through shared IndexedDB, main.ts:658-664);
- run launch sweeps;
- take the app's multi-window presence lock from the sweep branch without deciding to.

PER-UNIT RESET, each pinned by a test that runs unit A then unit B:
- the bash shell cache (tool.ts:39, :86), so unit A's /workspace file is absent in unit B;
- per D5, no /mnt mounts and no /chats projection for a phone shell;
- MCP client sessions (client.ts:44-46): reconnect per unit, or record why server-side session state is accepted;
- Router breaker and latency state (engine.ts:510-517): reset per unit, or accept and document;
- engine per-turn fields (engine.ts:503-506): assert one unit at a time;
- `cachedTokens` (inference-node llama-cpp.ts:577-596): never crosses to a phone, and the test asserts it is absent from the terminal;
- `approvals` (app.ts:417-441): never populated in the worker.

Also add a layering assertion that src/worker imports no @chatterang/desktop or tunnel host.

MUTATIONS
- Reuse the shell across units.
- Load chats in the worker.
- Forward cachedTokens.
- Build the engine with the settings' fallback.
Each must fail.

MUST STAY TRUE
- The user window's boot is byte-identical.
- API keys never enter the worker's shell VFS (stores.ts:71).
